inal example and locate the words or actions that support the idea. Before looking at the correction, make your own attempt using the exact question provided. Check your response against the feedback: did you address the same skill and show your reasoning? If a detail is uncertain, identify what would have to be checked. One deliberate, justified revision is more useful than making the answer longer.","icon":"📖","notice":"Repeating the worked example cannot show transfer to new content. Correct the meaning, not just the appearance.","title":"Transfer to an independent example"}],"title":"Year 3, Week 33, Lesson 3: Direct speech review","unit_number":7,"unit_title":"Myths, legends and First Nations stories","week":33,"week_in_unit":3,"word_challenges":null,"worked_example":"WORK THROUGH THIS\nCorrect: Lea said, \"The ford is higher up.\" The comma sits before the quote; the quoted sentence starts with a capital.\n\nExplain what makes this example accurate and effective, identifying its specific wording.","worked_visuals":[{"alt":"Direct speech punctuation with comma and capital.","caption":"Quoted sentences need end marks too.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#e8f5ed\" stroke=\"#297a61\"/><g font-size=\"16\" fill=\"#263948\"><text x=\"28\" y=\"42\">Speech marks</text><text x=\"28\" y=\"78\">&quot;The ford is higher up.&quot;</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"42\">Reporting comma</text><text x=\"358\" y=\"78\">Lea said,</text></g></svg>"},{"alt":"Excited quote with complete punctuation.","caption":"Hunt missing commas and capitals.","svg":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 660 150\"><rect x=\"10\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fill=\"#fff4ea\" stroke=\"#b87445\"/><rect x=\"340\" y=\"12\" width=\"310\" height=\"126\" rx=\"14\" fi